# Jirakli Project Conventions

Project-specific rules and patterns for the Jirakli codebase.

## Project Structure

```
jirakli/
├── package.json              # pnpm workspace root
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml
├── docker-compose.yml
├── Dockerfile
├── .env.example
├── packages/
│   ├── client/               # Angular 17+ application
│   ├── server/               # NestJS application
│   └── shared/               # Shared types, schemas, constants
└── data/                     # SQLite database (gitignored)
```

## Shared Package Usage

### Import Pattern
```typescript
// Always import from @jirakli/shared
import { Ticket, CreateTicketDto, TICKET_STATUS } from '@jirakli/shared';

// Never import directly from shared package internals
// Bad: import { Ticket } from '@jirakli/shared/src/schemas/ticket';
```

### What Goes in Shared
- Drizzle schemas and types
- Zod validation schemas
- DTOs (used by both client and server)
- Constants and enums
- Utility types

### What Doesn't Go in Shared
- Business logic
- Services
- Angular/NestJS specific code
- Environment configuration

## API Conventions

### URL Structure
```
/api/v1/auth/*           # Authentication
/api/v1/users/*          # User management
/api/v1/projects/*       # Projects
/api/v1/projects/:id/tickets/*  # Tickets (nested under project)
/api/v1/tickets/:id/*    # Direct ticket access (for updates/deletes)
/api/v1/tickets/:id/comments/*  # Comments
```

### Response Format
```typescript
// Success (single item)
{
  "data": { /* entity */ }
}

// Success (list)
{
  "data": [ /* entities */ ],
  "pagination": {
    "page": 1,
    "pageSize": 20,
    "total": 100,
    "totalPages": 5
  }
}

// Error
{
  "statusCode": 400,
  "message": "Validation failed",
  "errors": [
    { "field": "title", "message": "Title is required" }
  ],
  "timestamp": "2024-01-15T10:30:00Z"
}
```

### HTTP Status Codes
- `200` - Success (GET, PATCH)
- `201` - Created (POST)
- `204` - No Content (DELETE)
- `400` - Bad Request (validation errors)
- `401` - Unauthorized (not logged in)
- `403` - Forbidden (logged in but not allowed)
- `404` - Not Found
- `409` - Conflict (e.g., duplicate email)
- `500` - Internal Server Error

## Naming Conventions

### Ticket Numbers
Format: `{PROJECT_KEY}-{NUMBER}`
- Example: `JIR-42`, `PROJ-123`
- Numbers are sequential within a project
- Keys are uppercase, 2-6 characters

### IDs
- All IDs are UUIDs (stored as text in SQLite)
- Generate with `crypto.randomUUID()`
- Never use auto-increment IDs

### Timestamps
- Store as Unix milliseconds (`integer` in SQLite)
- Use `Date` objects in TypeScript
- Return as ISO 8601 strings in API responses

## Error Handling

### Service Layer
```typescript
// Throw NestJS built-in exceptions
throw new NotFoundException(`Ticket "${id}" not found`);
throw new BadRequestException('Invalid status transition');
throw new ForbiddenException('You cannot edit this ticket');
throw new ConflictException('Email already registered');

// Include context in message
throw new NotFoundException(`Project with key "${key}" not found`);
```

### Repository Layer
```typescript
// Return null for not found, let service decide
async findById(id: string): Promise<Ticket | null> {
  // ...
  return result[0] ?? null;
}

// Service handles the null
async getTicket(id: string): Promise<Ticket> {
  const ticket = await this.repository.findById(id);
  if (!ticket) {
    throw new NotFoundException(`Ticket "${id}" not found`);
  }
  return ticket;
}
```

### Frontend
```typescript
// Use Angular's HttpErrorResponse
this.ticketService.createTicket(dto).pipe(
  catchError((error: HttpErrorResponse) => {
    if (error.status === 400) {
      this.handleValidationErrors(error.error.errors);
    } else {
      this.toastService.error('Something went wrong');
    }
    return EMPTY;
  }),
);
```

## Authentication

### JWT Structure
```typescript
interface JwtPayload {
  sub: string;        // User ID
  email: string;
  iat: number;        // Issued at
  exp: number;        // Expiration
}
```

### Auth Flow
1. Login: `POST /api/v1/auth/login` → Returns JWT
2. Client stores JWT in memory (not localStorage for security)
3. Client sends JWT in `Authorization: Bearer {token}` header
4. Server validates JWT on protected routes

### Protected Routes
```typescript
// Server: Apply guard to controller or specific routes
@Controller('tickets')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)
export class TicketsController {}

// Client: Use HTTP interceptor to attach token
```

## State Management (Frontend)

### Use Signals for Component State
```typescript
@Component({...})
export class TicketListComponent {
  tickets = signal<Ticket[]>([]);
  loading = signal(false);
  error = signal<string | null>(null);
}
```

### Use Services with Signals for Shared State
```typescript
@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class AuthState {
  private _user = signal<User | null>(null);
  user = this._user.asReadonly();
  isAuthenticated = computed(() => this._user() !== null);
}
```

### Don't Use NgRx
For this project's scope, signals + services are sufficient. NgRx adds complexity we don't need.

## Testing Conventions

### File Naming
```
ticket.service.ts        → ticket.service.spec.ts
ticket-list.component.ts → ticket-list.component.spec.ts
```

### Test Utilities Location
```
packages/server/src/test/
├── utils.ts           # Test helpers
├── factories.ts       # Entity factories
└── mocks.ts           # Common mocks

packages/client/src/test/
├── utils.ts
├── factories.ts
└── mocks.ts
```

### Factory Pattern
```typescript
// packages/server/src/test/factories.ts
export function createMockTicket(overrides: Partial<Ticket> = {}): Ticket {
  return {
    id: crypto.randomUUID(),
    projectId: 'project-1',
    number: 1,
    title: 'Test Ticket',
    status: 'todo',
    priority: 'medium',
    reporterId: 'user-1',
    assigneeId: null,
    description: null,
    createdAt: new Date(),
    updatedAt: new Date(),
    ...overrides,
  };
}
```

## Git Conventions

### Branch Naming
```
feature/ticket-crud
fix/login-validation
refactor/auth-service
docs/api-readme
```

### Commit Messages
```
feat: add ticket creation endpoint
fix: correct status transition validation
refactor: extract ticket repository
docs: update API documentation
test: add ticket service unit tests
chore: update dependencies
```

### PR Requirements
- All tests pass
- No TypeScript errors
- Follows code style guidelines
- Has meaningful commit messages

## Environment Configuration

### Required Variables
```env
# .env.example
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key-min-32-chars

# Optional (defaults shown)
PORT=3000
DATABASE_PATH=./data/jirakli.db
```

### Access in Code
```typescript
// Server: Use ConfigService
@Injectable()
export class AuthService {
  constructor(private config: ConfigService) {}
  
  private get jwtSecret(): string {
    return this.config.getOrThrow('JWT_SECRET');
  }
}

// Client: Use environment files
// environments/environment.ts
export const environment = {
  apiUrl: '/api/v1',
};
```

## Docker Conventions

### Single Container
The app runs as a single container with:
- NestJS serving API on `/api/*`
- NestJS serving static Angular build on `/*`
- SQLite database in a mounted volume

### Volume Mount
```bash
docker run -v jirakli-data:/app/data jirakli
```

### Health Check
```
GET /api/v1/health → { "status": "ok", "timestamp": "..." }
```

## Performance Guidelines

### Pagination
- Default page size: 20
- Max page size: 100
- Always paginate list endpoints

### Eager Loading
```typescript
// Load relations when needed, not by default
const ticket = await db.query.tickets.findFirst({
  where: eq(tickets.id, id),
  with: { 
    assignee: true,
    reporter: true,
    // Only load comments if needed
  },
});
```

### Caching
Not implemented in MVP. When added:
- Use in-memory cache for SQLite (it's local anyway)
- Invalidate on writes
